fix(ui): F-0021 Dosing switch stays visible in forced-colours mode

Finding:     F-0021 (P1, A11Y-19 / WCAG 1.4.11; merged duplicates F-0026, F-0051):
             in Windows High Contrast / forced colours the switch track and knob and
             the sensor dots disappeared, so dosing on/off could not be seen.
Originating: forced-colours captures at 320 and 1280, default and manual-dosing: the
             switch is drawn and on/off differ; the dots are drawn.
Regression:  journey switch-dosing-to-manual; audit contrast,axe,keyboard,states;
             normal-mode captures unchanged; ARIA unchanged.
Drift class: local defect -> a forced-colors media block using system colours
             (off: Canvas track outlined in ButtonText, ButtonText knob at left;
              on: Highlight track, HighlightText knob at right).
Layer:       styles.css, new @media (forced-colors: active) block only.
Assumptions: none.
Left alone:  in forced colours all dots share one colour; statuses are told apart by
             the words added in F-0019.
Re-test:     run 20261007-101436-fix-f-0021: axe/keyboard/contrast/states 0, journey
             3/3; only the four forced-colours captures changed. PASSED.
Baseline:    665ca185ac74f08453715a82013e960438c2e377; apply after F-0003.

diff --git a/styles.css b/styles.css
index 3dc9552..5cdf60d 100644
--- a/styles.css
+++ b/styles.css
@@ -309,6 +309,36 @@ th {
   gap: 7px;
 }
 
+@media (forced-colors: active) {
+  .switch__track,
+  .switch__knob,
+  .dot {
+    forced-color-adjust: none;
+  }
+
+  .switch__track {
+    background: Canvas;
+    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 2px ButtonText;
+  }
+
+  .switch__knob {
+    background: ButtonText;
+  }
+
+  .switch[aria-checked="true"] .switch__track {
+    background: Highlight;
+    box-shadow: none;
+  }
+
+  .switch[aria-checked="true"] .switch__knob {
+    background: HighlightText;
+  }
+
+  .dot {
+    background: CanvasText;
+  }
+}
